{
    "background_story": "Kashton was a young M\u00e9tis trapper who lived in the vast wilderness of the Canadian North. He was known for his exceptional skills in the bush and his love for traditional cooking. Kashton's grandmother, a respected elder in their community, had taught him the art of making bannock - a delicious, flaky flatbread that was a staple in their culture. Whenever Kashton returned from a long hunting trip, he would make a big batch of bannock, sharing it with his family and friends. The smell of freshly baked bannock wafting from his cabin became a welcoming beacon, signaling to everyone that Kashton was home and ready to share stories of his adventures. As he traveled the land, Kashton would often share his bannock with other travelers, spreading warmth and kindness wherever he went.",
